model {
  extend basalt.poolDatabase {
    metadata {
      constraint "Private schema apply failures retain only validated SQLSTATE or connection codes, closed failure kinds and narrowly validated denied-resource identifiers. Driver messages, parameters, credentials and nested causes never enter diagnostics. Input validation, authorization and the empty public failure response stay unchanged. Named additive migrations keep change-feed invalidation at each legacy row-trigger snapshot, including its concurrent mapping creation miss; one resolution at statement end is rejected because a reader that registers after a mid-statement mapping delete keeps a stale count. A hash-only resolver uses covering hash indexes; target lists are never cached across rows. With the journal active, a row whose hash already bumped its pool and topic in the same transaction skips the repeated no-op journal inserts through a transaction-local memo that rolls back with them. UTF8 encoding is required so immutable byte hashing matches the existing UTF8 hash. Trigger definitions, indexes, UPDATE and DELETE watchers, journal writes and transaction boundaries remain unchanged; later migrations replace function bodies only and take no table lock. Index creation and function replacement commit atomically under bounded schema lock and statement timeouts."
    }
  }
}
